# One set of bytes on every machine. Signatures, hashes and gofmt all depend on it: a Windows checkout that turned LF into
# CRLF broke the golden signature test and made every Go file look unformatted.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.minisig -text
internal/sign/testdata/** -text
protocol/golden/** -text
*.exe binary
*.gguf binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.bat text eol=crlf
